{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-30009-r4630232","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Ambrosia Fruit Salad","sourcePageId":30009,"sourceRevision":"4630232","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-04-12T19:26:20Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Ambrosia%20Fruit%20Salad&oldid=4630232","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T12:22:52.393Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Halal recipes","Category:Kosher for Passover recipes","Category:Naturally gluten-free recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes using grape","Category:Recipes using marshmallow","Category:Recipes using orange","Category:Recipes using pineapple","Category:Recipes using whipped cream","Category:Recipes with images","Category:Refrigerated recipes","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"dbad5d988aa1dacd6cf926e93b9c5de53cdee1f994491ae7ed1453d64f055152","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary\n| category = Recipes for dessert\n| Cuisine = USA\n| servings = 8\n| time = Prep: 5 minutes<br/>Chilling: 60 minutes\n| difficulty = 1\n| Image = [[File:Ambrosia salad.jpg|300px]]\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Dessert|Dessert]]\n\n'''Ambrosia Fruit Salad''' is a sweet mixture of mandarin oranges, fruit cocktail, coconut, and marshmallows coated in whipped cream. It originated in the 1900s and had a period of popularity in the United States. It is widely considered to be a traditional dish, suitable for family gatherings. \n\nBelow is one interpretation.\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n*4 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] of [[Cookbook:Mandarin Orange|mandarin oranges]], drained\n*2 cans of [[Cookbook:Pineapple|pineapple]], drained\n*2 cups of [[Cookbook:Grape|grapes]]\n*3 cups [[Cookbook:Whipped Cream|whipped cream]]\n*1 cup [[Cookbook:Sour Cream|sour cream]]\n*6–8 cups miniature [[Cookbook:Marshmallow|marshmallows]]\n\n==Procedure==\n#Mix the mandarin oranges, pineapple, and grapes in a large bowl.\n#[[cookbook:Fold|Fold]] in the whipped cream, sour cream, and marshmallows.\n#Chill for at least an hour. \n#Stir again before serving.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Naturally gluten-free recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pineapple]]\n[[Category:Refrigerated recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using whipped cream]]\n[[Category:Recipes using orange]]\n[[Category:Recipes using grape]]\n[[Category:Recipes using marshmallow]]\n[[Category:Halal recipes]]\n[[Category:Kosher for Passover recipes]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Ambrosia Fruit Salad","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"8","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"4 cups of mandarin oranges, drained","sourceText":"4 cups of mandarin oranges, drained","amountText":"4 cups of mandarin oranges, drained","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"2 cans of pineapple, drained","sourceText":"2 cans of pineapple, drained","amountText":"2 cans of pineapple, drained","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"2 cups of grapes","sourceText":"2 cups of grapes","amountText":"2 cups of grapes","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"3 cups whipped cream","sourceText":"3 cups whipped cream","amountText":